  "data": {
    "body": "Three statements are given.\n\n(I) If $\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ and $\\{b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ are both convergent sequences, then $\\{a_n+b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ is a convergent sequence.\n\n(II) If $\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ and $\\{b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ are both divergent sequences, then $\\{a_n+b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ is a divergent sequence.\n\n(III) If $\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ is a convergent sequence and $\\{b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ is a divergent sequence, then $\\{a_n+b_n\\}_{n=1}^{\\infty}$ is a divergent sequence.\nSelect all TRUE statement(s) from above.",
